    "summary":  "The fifth Savior\u0027s location is revealed not in distant lands but through a beer can run over by a taxi—VALIS\u0027s bizarre communication method. The protagonist watches VALIS again and recognizes its subliminal message-firing technique, which validates Fat\u0027s March 1974 experience as real rather than delusional. The group grapples with the terrifying implications: apostolic Christians with advanced technology breached the space-time barrier, the immortal plásmate seeks vengeance against Nixon\u0027s America, and they possess dangerous knowledge that could prove fatal. Fat and the narrator prepare contact with Eric Lampton through a screenplay pretext, planning to deliver VALIS\u0027s cypher \u0027KING FELIX.\u0027 Lampton responds with just the word KING, the narrator completes it with FELIX, confirming linked contact. Eric calls at 2 A.M. and confirms the Savior is alive—a child who has slept for nearly two thousand years now awakening. The cypher meanings unwind: FELIX (prosperous, fertile, happy, successful) points to legitimate rule replacing tyranny. The group forms the Rhipidon Society and prepares to travel to Sonoma to meet Eric and Linda Lampton.",
